{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cff3CejSNKmq24HxMn91V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate **`gist_typicality_count_runs`**, and it passes the self-check (`OK`). The smoke-fit ELPD-LOO was −2956.1, about 566 nats behind the incumbent's −2390.1, so it will probably lose. The brief asked for a simpler, higher-variance hypothesis, and a clear loss is still informative.\n\n**Hypothesis:** people keep only a rough gist of each sequence: how many heads it has and how many runs it breaks into. A sequence looks random to the extent that many fair-coin sequences of the same length share that gist. Lopsided counts, long streaks (few runs) and strict alternation (the most runs possible) are all rare gists, so they look non-random. Balanced sequences with a middling number of runs are common, so they look random.\n\nThis is aimed at the two strongest problems in the critique. People pick the more balanced sequence when switch counts are equal (z=7.22), and they pick the sequence with the shorter longest run when switch counts are equal (z=6.21). A single typicality score can produce both, with no separate cues added.\n\n**Model:**\n- The feature is the difference between the two sequences in log(number of sequences with the same head count and run count). It is computed exactly by listing every sequence up to length 8.\n- Each person has their own sensitivity. It sits on a log scale with a population distribution, 400 slots and a non-centred setup, so the next design can still predict new participants.\n- `p_left` = sigmoid(sensitivity × typicality difference).\n\n**What the check doesn't cover:**\n- The smoke fit ran only one chain, so convergence (R-hat) was not verified.\n- PSIS-LOO came out unreliable on the smoke fit: 1.7% of trials had a high Pareto k, above the 1.0% tolerance. The ELPD estimate may therefore be off, and admission may flag the fit as untrusted.\n- Novelty against the other models was not checked.\n\nThe three files (`hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt`, `candidate.py`) are in `experiment2/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_1/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2624,"cache_read_input_tokens":56757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2624,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":696,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05a9ec81-607f-43b3-bb76-b6f86ab92976","uuid":"05622f93-703a-4eab-b5d1-7cf4e8a6e8ba","timestamp":"2026-10-03T09:07:00.386Z","request_id":"req_011Cff3CdBAe6fP9fPVy4Q7f"}
